      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "to simple words, and not to compounds. Vámana remarks-भवार्थे",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "पुनर्दिगादिपाठेपि वंशशब्दस्य वंशशब्दादेव तत्र प्रत्ययः । ग्रहणवता प्रातिपदिकेन",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "तदन्तविधेः प्रतिषेधात् । The form may be defended by explaining",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "it as तुल्यकुले साधवः, यत् being affixed by ‘तत्र साधु.’ Pân. IV. 4. 98.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 25. हिम०—कणशीकर v. l.; here कण means a drop and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "शीकर spray. हिमवतः स्थानानि—retreats in the Himàlayas, the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "favourite haunts of ascetics. सावमान &c.—see com.; given with,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "accompanied by, indignities; or सावमानं यथा स्यात्तथा with humi-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "liation. रताः—take pleasure in.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 26. कन्दर—the slopes between two hills; see sl. 79.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "प्रसभं—प्रगता सभा विचारोऽस्मात् तद्यथा तथा । forcibly i. e. against",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "one’s thoughts, or wishes. This may also be taken with अपगत०.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "प्रश्रय—courtesy, courteous behaviour. ‘प्रश्रयप्रणयौ समौ’ Amara.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "The last line is adj. to मुखानि.—लतानि—This refers to the eye-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "brows of men proud of their wealth which are sometimes raised,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "at others wrinkled. Cf. Bhàg. II. 2-5. quoted in the com.,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "reading the 3rd and 4th lines as रुद्धा गुहाः किमजितोऽवति नोपसन्नान्",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "कस्माद्भजन्ति &c.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl 27. The reading प्रिय has been adopted in this ed.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "instead of प्रिये, as mas. vocatives often occur, while a female is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "rarely addressed in this Sátaka. प्रणयिनि violates the metre.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "प्रणयिनीं—must be taken with वृत्ति some how. Another reading",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "is प्रियैश्च सलिलैः; but this, too, is not satisfactory, as there is no",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "propriety of प्रियैः. अकरुण v. l.—not pleasing, harsh to the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "touch; rough. यामः is replaced by यावः which is found in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "one ed. ईश्वराणां—goes with नामापि, and means ‘of rich people’;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "cf. ( Mis. sl. 11.) वित्त &c.—विकाराः such as rudeness, vanity &c.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "Mr. Telang’s reading is चित्तव्याधि which is redundant as we",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "have already got विवेकमूढ. For the idea cf. Mis. sl. 32.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 28. प्रतिवनम्—in every forest. अखेदम्—an adj. ( Bah com. )",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "or adv. For the idea expressed here comp. infra Sl. 55.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 29. दर्घन्ते—appear long. The man who has the misery to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "supplicate the rich, often in vain, finds the days very long. आक्षेप",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
